[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to an Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises because the API design allows direct access to images through their identifiers (`imageId`) without implementing proper access control mechanisms. If the `imageId` is predictable or not sufficiently protected, unauthorized users could potentially access or manipulate images that they are not authorized to view, leading to a breach of confidentiality or exposure of sensitive data. This issue is caused by the lack of authentication or authorization checks when accessing resources via the `/images/{imageId}` endpoint.

